      "id": 1,
      "text": "Manly was originally called Manly Junction and was laid out in 1877 at the intersection of the Rock Island and Chicago Great Western railroads.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manly%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name honors Central of Iowa freight agent J.C., who helped establish the junction that became Manly.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://cityofmanly.com/history/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A 1914 Sanborn Fire Insurance Map of Manly is one of only three historic maps available, offering a detailed view of the town’s early layout.",
